her Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "51540"} "1908"] "\n" [:option {:value "51570"} "1912"] "\n" [:option {:value "51598"} "1920"] "\n" [:option {:value "51627"} "1924"] "\n" [:option {:value "51648"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "51661"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "51692"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "51707"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "51899"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "51950"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "52011"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "261399"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "321052"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "395723"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "18000737"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2013117"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/494"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Trap, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "15 – 17 July 1900 — 9:00"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/207"} "Le Stand de l'Île Séguin, Billancourt"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/51514"} "31 from 5 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "20 shots."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The details of the 1900 trap shooting are not well known. The first and second places came down to a shoot-off between a Frenchman, " [:a {:href "/athletes/42116"} "Roger de Barbarin"] ", and Belgium’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/42164"} "René Guyot"] ", who tied at 17 each. De Barbarin won 13-12 in the shoot-off .Third went to " [:a {:href "/athletes/42123"} "Justinien, Count Clary"] ", a French shooter who also scored 17, but missed on his second attempt in the sudden death shoot-off. Count Clary later served on the " [:a {:href "/organizations/1"} "IOC"] " from 1919-33. " [:a {:href "/athletes/1200825"} "David Wallechinsky"] ", in " [:strong {} [:em {} "The Complete Book of the Olympics"]] ", notes that de Barbarin was described as a man with “a piercing gaze and a delicate black moustache”."] "\n\n" [:p {} "While the other seven shooting events of the Paris Olympics also doubled as the World Championships, this was not the case for the trap shooting. This was to be the first and only time the World Championships were held concurrently with the Olympics, and the Olympic Champions also became World Champions. It was the fourth staging of the World Championships, having previously been held in Lyon (France) in 1897, Turin (Italy) in 1898, and Loosduinen in 1899 (which, since 1923, has been a district of Den Haag, in the Netherlands). But this did not apply to trap, which was not seen at the World Championships until Stockholm in 1929."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Shoot-Off"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/42116"} "Roger de Barbarin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "17"] [:td {} "13"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/42164"} "René Guyot"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BEL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BEL.png"}] "BEL"]] [:td {} "17"] [:td {} "12"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/42123"} "Justinien, Comte Clary"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https:/